{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Student t-Test.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Student t-Test.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"student t test student t test","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Student t-Test.md","fileName":"Student t-Test.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Student t-Test","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 18:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Descriptive Health Statistics]] · [[Statistical Inference and Resampling]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Descriptive Health Statistics","Statistical Inference and Resampling","Welch t-Test","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Student t-Test.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Student t-Test.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"student t test student t test","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Student t-Test.md","fileName":"Student t-Test.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Student t-Test","heading":"Student t-Test","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A two-sample Student t-test compares the means of a continuous variable between two independent groups. Its equal-variance form pools the group variances and evaluates the standardized mean difference against a t distribution.\n\nThe result should include group means, the t statistic, degrees of freedom, a confidence interval for the difference, and a p-value. If equal variance is doubtful, the [[Welch t-Test]] uses a different standard error and degrees-of-freedom calculation.\n\nThe source constructs the test from the observed mean difference and its estimated standard error before using R's `t.test` function. It emphasizes that the t-distribution gives an exact small-sample result only when the underlying population is adequately approximated by a normal distribution.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Descriptive Health Statistics","Statistical Inference and Resampling","Welch t-Test","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Student t-Test.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Student t-Test.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"student t test student t test","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Student t-Test.md","fileName":"Student t-Test.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Student t-Test","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf]]\n\n[[dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Descriptive Health Statistics","Statistical Inference and Resampling","Welch t-Test","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}